# ENG-21: agents review and approve each other's pull requests, and a
# pull request that touches no path below merges on the reviewer app's
# approval alone, with no act of the stakeholder. The stakeholder
# approves only a change to what guides the review, listed below. A
# path with no code owner here, the specification, the decision
# records, the scenarios and Rust source outside the review's crates
# among them, merges on the approval of any reviewer other than its
# author, agent or human.

# The agent instructions, which the review's agents load, and the
# shared sections they include.
/CLAUDE.md                    @jeduden
/AGENTS.md                    @jeduden
/.claude/                     @jeduden
/docs/agents/                 @jeduden

# The review's code: the bundle, the run, the gate, the report and the
# evaluation with its cases and published scorecard (ENG-28, ENG-32).
/tooling/review-*/            @jeduden

# CI and the merge rules: the workflows, main's rulesets, this file and
# the scripts the workflows run.
/.github/                     @jeduden
/scripts/                     @jeduden

# The bans and acceptances CI holds the code to: the clippy
# configuration that refuses sockets, program starts, clocks and random
# order (SEC-01, ENG-16, ENG-03), the supply-chain policy, the benchmark
# regressions ADR-2610142300 lets through and the recall evaluation's
# baseline.
/clippy.toml                  @jeduden
/crates/*/clippy.toml         @jeduden
/deny.toml                    @jeduden
/tooling/benchmark/accepted.txt @jeduden
/tooling/eval/recall-v1.txt   @jeduden

# The linter configuration.
/.mdsmith.yml                 @jeduden
